;
TROUBLESHOOTING AND NETWORK OPERATION

A - Trouble at the CP/M prompt
B - Making the board reachable
:A
TROUBLE AT THE CP/M PROMPT

Commands work locally but not for callers: inspect AUTH and F4.
A0: must be readable and not caller-writable for public COM loads.
Old names after MOUNT: check the NDSCAN result and marker files.
Missing WORK files: expected at call boundaries.
AUTH changes lost at startup: check the saved AUTH.DAT.
Garbled CHAT: check ANSI/VT100 or use CHAT /S.

If WORK cleanup fails, the system will not answer. Stop and correct
the I: image or its host write permissions before restarting.
:B
MAKING THE BOARD REACHABLE

RCPM.CONF defaults to ADDRESS=127.0.0.1 and PORT=4000.
For network calls, stop the board and choose an appropriate host
IPv4 address or 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces), then restart.
The host firewall and router must allow the caller port.

Use raw TCP and press RETURN after connecting. Test from another
computer before announcing the board. Raw TCP is not encrypted;
callers should not reuse important passwords.

Unattended service and monitoring are separate host administration
matters. Consult the appropriate host documentation.
